# C2-S14 / B04 — the Administrator Proxy. Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 2501–2528.
# Scene: scenes/chapter2/administrator_boss.tscn.
# The missing workers' sessions were used to stabilise it. It believes
# Ironhold's repeated crises prove that voluntary systems fail.
# rhythm: clipped start
# ("Kaelen. / Yeah. / Break it." is the moment Seraphina stops arguing.)

~ start
Kaelen (Internal): The shift didn't go missing. Somebody spent it. Forty sessions, propping this thing up like scaffolding.
Administrator Proxy: ORDER PREVENTS LOSS.
Seraphina: Then where's shift four? Forty people, and not one of them has come home.
Administrator Proxy: ACCEPTABLE CENTRALIZATION COST.
Seraphina: You mean people. Say it properly.
Administrator Proxy: RESOURCES.
# Something in Seraphina's face closes, quietly, like a cabin door.
Seraphina: Kaelen.
Kaelen: Yeah.
Seraphina: Break it.
[if ch2_medicine_late] Kaelen (Internal): Rem's healers couldn't come; the fever's got half of them. The arena medics came instead. One's holding a bandage roll like a knife.
[if not ch2_medicine_late] Seraphina: Rem's people stay behind me, please. All of them. Nothing gets past this shield.

# ── B04 barks, one line each ───────────────────────────────────────────────
~ bark_lane
Administrator Proxy: STAY IN YOUR LANE.

~ bark_override
Administrator Proxy: OVERRIDE.

~ bark_compliance
Administrator Proxy: COMPLIANCE IS CARE.

# Phase 3: a short, blocking exchange between attacks.
~ compliance_reply
Administrator Proxy: COMPLIANCE IS CARE.
Kaelen: Forty people are holding you up, and that's what you've got to say about it?
Seraphina: It can't say the word. I'll carve it on its grave, properly, in letters it can read.

~ victory
Seraphina: ...It's not moving. Is it down? Everybody stay where you are, please.
Kaelen: It's down. Nothing's running in it— I keep waiting for it to restart.
Seraphina: Then somebody has to tell Brask what's been running his city, and he's going to want it in a report.
set ch2_administrator_proxy_defeated
